635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430371 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430377 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430381 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1077 "selection" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430371 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430388 1079 #uuid "922f5d01-e962-51be-9d91-e5c9f7c8303a" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430389 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430387 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430389 1069 "q-90562" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430389 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430389 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430389 1072 #uuid "30cb3fc9-0bbc-51d2-bbe4-e74999cc9efd" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430389 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{45})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{30})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}-{(\\frac{11}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{50} \\\\  & =0.66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430390 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430385 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430390 1069 "q-131262" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430390 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430390 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{6},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430390 1072 #uuid "572f0ee2-d90d-5ec7-a063-65cce5fd61fa" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430390 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{8}|}_{0}^{1}+(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}){|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{72}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430391 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430386 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430391 1069 "q-90539" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430391 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430391 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{17}{24},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430391 1072 #uuid "5874ecb6-66d6-5729-9147-ef1e0e5bab53" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430391 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-{(\\frac{17}{24})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{143}{576} \\\\  & ≈0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430392 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430388 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430392 1069 "q-131167" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430392 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430392 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430392 1072 #uuid "6332f216-e713-5bbb-8f9f-dbf095406d20" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true] [17592186430392 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{x}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{18}|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =12-{(3)}^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534635 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0e83b986-ddee-59b4-802a-948fde980775" 17592186430365 "answer-1204147e-9d6e-5e43-8474-be634d7db4f2" 17592186430366 "answer-1efa5566-7842-5b7d-abc6-3035b571fbef" 